<programme start="20261015150000 +0000" stop="20261015160000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Southern Hoops: A History of SEC Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Part Two (1960-1970)</sub-title><desc lang="en">Texas Western&apos;s historic win over Adolph Rupp&apos;s Kentucky team in the 1966 NCAA final marks a turning point in the SEC. Vanderbilt&apos;s Perry Wallace becomes the conference&apos;s first Black player, while at LSU, Pete Maravich rewrites the record books.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p23827470_b_h8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261015160000 +0000" stop="20261015170000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Southern Hoops: A History of SEC Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Part Three (1971-1979)</sub-title><desc lang="en">Dale Brown brings an infectious personality to LSU while Pat Summitt begins her legendary coaching career at Tennessee. And the year after Adolph Rupp&apos;s death in 1977, his successor Joe B. Hall leads Kentucky to its first NCAA title in 20 years.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p23827470_b_h8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261015170000 +0000" stop="20261015180000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">Southern Hoops: A History of SEC Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Part Four (1980-1989)</sub-title><desc lang="en">Georgia&apos;s Dominique Wilkins and Auburn&apos;s Charles Barkley headline the SEC&apos;s successes in the early 1980s, while LSU&apos;s Dale Brown takes two teams to the Final Four. Pat Summitt wins her first two national titles at Tennessee.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p23827470_b_v12_ab.jpg"/></programme>
